1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:07,544
Hi! Welcome to our ribbon plaza. Let's count Catalan numbers, and watch the equations make each new value.

2
00:00:08,144 --> 00:00:13,916
A ribbon can go up and down. It starts on this line, finishes on the line, and never goes below it.

3
00:00:14,516 --> 00:00:20,828
One up step and one down step make a pair. Catalan numbers count the different paths for each number of pairs.

4
00:00:21,428 --> 00:00:28,151
With no pairs, there is one empty path. An empty path still counts as one choice. Our first value is one.

5
00:00:28,751 --> 00:00:35,090
The small label tells us the number of pairs. The big number tells us how many paths. They tell us different things.

6
00:00:35,690 --> 00:00:42,683
We will count from C zero to C thirty. First we will see the paths, then a quicker equation will make the growing values.

7
00:00:43,283 --> 00:00:43,758
one

8
00:00:44,358 --> 00:00:53,019
To move one place forward, take the last value, multiply by four times the new label minus two, then divide by the new label plus one.

9
00:00:53,619 --> 00:01:02,870
Always multiply first. The middle window shows the whole product. Then divide that product into equal shares. One share gives the next Catalan number.

10
00:01:03,470 --> 00:01:11,704
These number windows show values. The ribbons point to the calculation; they are not a picture of every path when the numbers become large.

11
00:01:13,704 --> 00:01:16,295
one times two, divided by two, equals.

12
00:01:16,455 --> 00:01:16,931
one

13
00:01:17,531 --> 00:01:25,689
We have one and one. The first belongs to no pairs; the second belongs to one pair. Same value, different places. Keep both.

14
00:01:26,289 --> 00:01:32,662
For one pair, the only path goes up, then down. Its two ends touch the line. There is exactly one way.

15
00:01:34,662 --> 00:01:37,340
one times six, divided by three, equals.

16
00:01:37,500 --> 00:01:38,016
two

17
00:01:38,616 --> 00:01:45,524
For two pairs, we can climb twice and come down twice, or make two little peaks. Different paths, the same number of pairs.

18
00:01:47,524 --> 00:01:50,202
two times ten, divided by four, equals.

19
00:01:50,362 --> 00:01:50,962
five

20
00:01:51,562 --> 00:01:59,663
Here are all five paths for three pairs. Watch the first step up. Follow its matching step down: that is the first return to the line.

21
00:02:00,263 --> 00:02:08,413
Inside this first arch is a smaller path. After the arch is another path. Choose the inside and the part after it, then join them.

22
00:02:09,013 --> 00:02:17,396
If the inside has no pairs, the part after has two. One choice times two choices gives two paths. Both belong in this first group.

23
00:02:17,996 --> 00:02:26,189
One pair inside and one after gives one times one: one path. Two pairs inside and none after gives two times one: two paths.

24
00:02:26,789 --> 00:02:34,686
Add the three groups: two plus one plus two makes five. Each path has only one first return, so every path appears once.

25
00:02:36,686 --> 00:02:39,722
five times fourteen, divided by five, equals.

26
00:02:39,882 --> 00:02:40,585
fourteen

27
00:02:41,185 --> 00:02:51,126
Look back at our equation. Five times fourteen made seventy. Dividing seventy into five equal shares gave fourteen in each share. Nothing was rounded.

28
00:02:51,726 --> 00:03:00,846
The path rule and this arithmetic rule give the same Catalan numbers. We can follow the small paths, and use exact arithmetic as the values grow.

29
00:03:02,846 --> 00:03:06,025
fourteen times eighteen, divided by six, equals.

30
00:03:06,185 --> 00:03:06,977
forty-two

31
00:03:08,977 --> 00:03:12,463
forty-two times twenty-two, divided by seven, equals.

32
00:03:12,623 --> 00:03:13,985
one hundred thirty-two

33
00:03:15,985 --> 00:03:20,097
one hundred thirty-two times twenty-six, divided by eight, equals.

34
00:03:20,257 --> 00:03:21,613
four hundred twenty-nine

35
00:03:23,613 --> 00:03:27,638
four hundred twenty-nine times thirty, divided by nine, equals.

36
00:03:27,798 --> 00:03:29,517
one thousand four hundred thirty

37
00:03:31,517 --> 00:03:36,107
one thousand four hundred thirty times thirty-four, divided by ten, equals.

38
00:03:36,267 --> 00:03:38,235
four thousand eight hundred sixty-two

39
00:03:40,235 --> 00:03:45,300
four thousand eight hundred sixty-two times thirty-eight, divided by eleven, equals.

40
00:03:45,460 --> 00:03:47,741
sixteen thousand seven hundred ninety-six

41
00:03:48,341 --> 00:03:58,464
Sixteen thousand, seven hundred ninety-six. We are counting ways, not drawing that many ribbons. The smaller paths still explain why each new value belongs here.

42
00:04:00,464 --> 00:04:06,075
sixteen thousand seven hundred ninety-six times forty-two, divided by twelve, equals.

43
00:04:06,235 --> 00:04:08,510
fifty-eight thousand seven hundred eighty-six

44
00:04:10,510 --> 00:04:16,285
fifty-eight thousand seven hundred eighty-six times forty-six, divided by thirteen, equals.

45
00:04:16,445 --> 00:04:18,107
two hundred eight thousand twelve

46
00:04:20,107 --> 00:04:24,739
two hundred eight thousand twelve times fifty, divided by fourteen, equals.

47
00:04:24,899 --> 00:04:27,288
seven hundred forty-two thousand nine hundred

48
00:04:29,288 --> 00:04:34,984
seven hundred forty-two thousand nine hundred times fifty-four, divided by fifteen, equals.

49
00:04:35,144 --> 00:04:38,492
two million six hundred seventy-four thousand four hundred forty

50
00:04:40,492 --> 00:04:47,316
two million six hundred seventy-four thousand four hundred forty times fifty-eight, divided by sixteen, equals.

51
00:04:47,476 --> 00:04:51,569
nine million six hundred ninety-four thousand eight hundred forty-five

52
00:04:52,169 --> 00:05:00,839
The numbers need more room now. We will open the whole screen for the value, while the multiplication and division keep their own clearly labeled windows.

53
00:05:02,839 --> 00:05:10,443
nine million six hundred ninety-four thousand eight hundred forty-five times sixty-two, divided by seventeen, equals.

54
00:05:10,603 --> 00:05:14,871
thirty-five million three hundred fifty-seven thousand six hundred seventy

55
00:05:16,871 --> 00:05:24,587
thirty-five million three hundred fifty-seven thousand six hundred seventy times sixty-six, divided by eighteen, equals.

56
00:05:24,747 --> 00:05:29,470
one hundred twenty-nine million six hundred forty-four thousand seven hundred ninety

57
00:05:31,470 --> 00:05:39,302
one hundred twenty-nine million six hundred forty-four thousand seven hundred ninety times seventy, divided by nineteen, equals.

58
00:05:39,462 --> 00:05:44,111
four hundred seventy-seven million six hundred thirty-eight thousand seven hundred

59
00:05:46,111 --> 00:05:54,092
four hundred seventy-seven million six hundred thirty-eight thousand seven hundred times seventy-four, divided by twenty, equals.

60
00:05:54,252 --> 00:06:00,101
one billion seven hundred sixty-seven million two hundred sixty-three thousand one hundred ninety

61
00:06:02,101 --> 00:06:11,539
one billion seven hundred sixty-seven million two hundred sixty-three thousand one hundred ninety times seventy-eight, divided by twenty-one, equals.

62
00:06:11,699 --> 00:06:16,686
six billion five hundred sixty-four million one hundred twenty thousand four hundred twenty

63
00:06:17,286 --> 00:06:25,410
The commas separate groups of three digits. Read each group with its place name. The commas help us read; they do not change the value.

64
00:06:27,410 --> 00:06:35,963
six billion five hundred sixty-four million one hundred twenty thousand four hundred twenty times eighty-two, divided by twenty-two, equals.

65
00:06:36,123 --> 00:06:41,292
twenty-four billion four hundred sixty-six million two hundred sixty-seven thousand twenty

66
00:06:43,292 --> 00:06:52,199
twenty-four billion four hundred sixty-six million two hundred sixty-seven thousand twenty times eighty-six, divided by twenty-three, equals.

67
